## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to combine TLS edge proxying with per-tenant feature gates loaded from a daemon-managed config source. It also checks bootstrap discipline in a two-DC setup.

## Key Concepts
- Docker Configs for runtime config
- TLS termination at Nginx edge proxy
- Per-tenant feature gates in a small API
- Simple bootstrap for tenants and flags

## Code Example
```javascript
const fs = require('fs');
const yaml = require('js-yaml');
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
let flags = {};
function loadFlags() {
  const txt = fs.readFileSync('/etc/feature-flags.yaml','utf8');
  flags = yaml.load(txt) || {};
}
loadFlags();
app.get('/health-quiz', (req, res) => {
  const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant-id'];
  if (tenant && flags[tenant] && flags[tenant].enabled) res.sendStatus(200);
  else res.sendStatus(403);
});
app.listen(3000);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test this gating with CI and two data centers?
- What are failure modes if the config-loader container is unavailable?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to implement a policy-driven, per-tenant response shaping mechanism in a docker-dca setup, using a Config object propagated to the service. It demonstrates practical data-safety concerns and integration with Traefik TLS termination.

## Key Concepts

- Docker Config for policy data
- Per-tenant response shaping and JSON filtering
- Payload transformation without altering business logic
- Traefik TLS edge in multi-DC deployments
- Basic end-to-end testing in a docker-dca context

## Code Example

```go
// Go example: filterFields filters payload by allowed keys
func filterFields(in map[string]interface{}, allowed []string) map[string]interface{} {
    out := make(map[string]interface{})
    set := make(map[string]struct{}, len(allowed))
    for _, k := range allowed { set[k] = struct{}{} }
    for k, v := range in {
        if _, ok := set[k]; ok {
            out[k] = v
        }
    }
    return out
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test for a tenant with no allowed fields? What would the response look like?
- What are the security implications if the tenant config is mis-synced between DCs, and how would you detect/mitigate it?
